  "poe": {
    "budgetW": 170,
    "sourceUrl": "https://static.us.zyxel.com/pdf/2024/switch/ds_GS1900-10HP.pdf",
    "note": "IEEE 802.3at PoE+ on all twenty-four copper ports at up to 30 W per port against a 170 W budget: 24 ports advertise 720 W of capability that the 170 W supply cannot deliver, so at most five ports run at the full 30 W at once. Firmware 2.90(ABTP.3)C0, released 2026-10-22, is the current release listed for this model on Zyxel download library https://www.zyxel.com/uk/en-gb/support/download?model=gs1900-24hpv2; the build code is per model (ABTP here) so the version string does not transfer verbatim to the other GS1900 members. The series user guide is V2.90 Edition 2 https://download.zyxel.com/GS1900-48HPv2/user_guide/GS1900-48HPv2_V2.90_Ed2.pdf."
  },
  "fabric": {
    "capacityMbps": 52000,
    "kind": "switching capacity",
    "note": "Zyxel quotes 52 Gbps switching capacity and 39 Mpps forwarding rate, with a 525 K packet buffer, an 8 K MAC address table and 9 K jumbo frames."
  },
  "sourceUrl": "https://static.us.zyxel.com/pdf/2024/switch/ds_GS1900-10HP.pdf",
  "notes": "Zyxel GS1900 Series datasheet (dated 16/11/22) https://static.us.zyxel.com/pdf/2024/switch/ds_GS1900-10HP.pdf; specification table https://www.zyxel.com/global/en/products/switch/gs1900-series/specification. Management and switching features from the datasheet feature list and the GS1900 Series User Guide V2.90 Edition 2 https://download.zyxel.com/GS1900-48HPv2/user_guide/GS1900-48HPv2_V2.90_Ed2.pdf. There is NO console port and no CLI anywhere in the series: management is the web GUI, SNMP v1/v2/v3, RMON 1/2/3/9, syslog, LLDP/LLDP-MED, 802.1x, RADIUS and TACACS+, which is why no device here declares cli. Twenty-four-port PoE model with uplinks: total port count 26 = 24 PoE RJ45 + 2 SFP, 170 W budget, 206.5 W maximum consumption, 441 x 270 x 44 mm, 3.55 kg, smart fan (22.1 dBA idle / 45.4 dBA maximum). The datasheet ordering table lists GS190024HPV2-EU0101F / -US0101F at hardware revision B1. The v2 suffix matters: the plain GS1900-24HP is a different chassis and is not modelled here."
}
